# Volkswagen Up! three-door hatchback, 2011-2023.
#
# The Up!: the small rear-engined-style city car with the upright body, the
# short overhangs and the simple interior. UK order books opened in October
# 2011. The five-door, e-Up! and GTI are variants on the same shell and are
# not separately represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volkswagen_Up
#
# Dimensions 3.540 x 1.641 x 1.480 m, wheelbase 2.420 m (three-door; the
# five-door is 3.563 m).
#
# Shape reference: NO true side elevation exists. Image 1 is about 25
# degrees off the flank; the front overhang must not be measured from it, as
# the notes warn. Images 2-3 show the front and rear. The limitation is
# recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no Volkswagen UK colour chart was read. White, black,
# silver and blue are plain names. Weights 12, 10, 10, 8, total 40,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 160 km/h. Comfort 65/428, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 65. Classes 0,1.
# Dates are road presence: 2011 intro, retires staggered 2034-2037.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vw-up.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/vw-up.dae. References:
# citycars/references/vw-up/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: there is no true side view, so the flank is estimated;
# the nose is more faceted and the rear slightly more tapered than the
# photographs. At 128 px the upright body, short overhangs and simple nose read
# as an Up!.


obj=citycar
name=VWUp(White)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=12
intro_year=2011
intro_month=10
retire_year=2037
retire_month=6
speed=160
class=0,1
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=65
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=428

